    "notes": [
      "The three-step crop sequence (3, 4 and 5 columns; 3, 4 and 6 rows) carries the idea well. The steps are uneven, though: far to mid adds one column and one row, while mid to near adds one column and two rows. Make the progression regular, for example cols 1–3/rows 5–7, cols 4–7/rows 5–8, cols 8–12/rows 5–9. Alternatively, push the near frame to rows 5–11 so the final step clearly reads as the arrival.",
      "Photo-near at 3.2× is visibly soft. The doorway in the final module looks pixelated at 5 columns × 6 rows. Use a higher-resolution source, or cap the near crop so it renders sharply.",
      "Photo-mid is 4 columns wide, but the gap between it and photo-near reads wider than the 12 pt gutter. Check that photo-mid ends exactly at the column 7 edge and photo-near starts at column 8. Do the same for the col 3/4 gap.",
      "Place-label sits under photo-far in row 8, but there is a one-row empty pocket below it in columns 1–3 while photo-mid runs to row 8. Move the label onto the first baseline directly under photo-far, hanging from the bottom of row 7, so it reads as that image's caption rather than floating.",
      "Lead spans cols 1–6, so it runs past photo-mid's right edge at col 7 and almost touches the col 8 photo. Narrow it to cols 1–6 with the rag held clear of the col 7 gutter, or set it to cols 1–5 to match the body measure. This gives the left text stack one consistent column edge.",
      "Body ends in row 11, leaving row 12 in cols 1–7 empty, and the space feels accidental. Either start body one row higher, right after the lead, or keep the empty row 12 and use it deliberately by aligning body's last line with county-label's baseline in row 11.",
      "County-label in cols 8–12 row 11 duplicates the footer's county and country fields. Replace it with a caption that names the step, e.g. 'The doors, St Ignatius Walk', so the third frame lands the idea.",
      "The headline across cols 1–12 / rows 2–4 dominates correctly. Tighten its baseline so the descender-free word sits on the row 4 bottom line, and leave exactly one baseline before the photos start in row 5.",
      "Number markers 1–3 sit at slightly different offsets inside each frame (marker 3 is lower relative to the frame edge). Pin all three to the same baseline-and-gutter inset from each photo's bottom-left corner."
    ],
    "summary": "The idea is clear and is expressed directly through spans: one photo zooming across 3→4→5 columns. The structure mostly holds, but the zoom steps are irregular, the near crop is too low-res, and the lead's measure and the right-hand caption weaken the grid's discipline. Regularise the step sizes, anchor the captions to their photos, and align the text column edges.",
    "mean": 7.2
  },
